Step 1:
We start by taking the first step in the Euclidean algorithm: subtract the initial two terms. Notice that
\begin{align*}a_{n+1} - (n+1)a_n &= (n+1)! + n + 1 - (n+1)(n! + n) \\ &= (n+1)! + n + 1 - (n+1)! - n(n+1) \\ &= -n^2 + 1 = -(n-1)(n+1).
\end{align*}

Step 2:
It follows that by the Euclidean Algorithm, 
\begin{align*}\text{gcd}\,(a_n, a_{n+1}) &= \text{gcd}\,(a_n, a_{n+1} - (n+1)a_n)\\ &= \text{gcd}\,(a_n, (n-1)(n+1)),\end{align*}
since the minus sign is irrelevant for calculating the gcd.

