Step 4:
Split the radicals:  
\begin{align*}
&= \sqrt{2}\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}}.
\end{align*}

Step 5:
Combine like terms and solve:  
\begin{align*}
\sqrt{2}\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}}+ \sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}} &= 2+2\sqrt{2}\\
\end{align*}

Step 6:
Factor out common terms:  
\begin{align*}
\Rightarrow \qquad (1+\sqrt{2})\sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}} &=2(1+\sqrt{2})\\
\end{align*}

Step 7:
Simplify the equation:  
\begin{align*}
\Rightarrow \qquad \sqrt{2+\sqrt{2+c}} &= 2\\
\end{align*}

Step 8:
Square both sides:  
\begin{align*}
\Rightarrow \qquad 2+\sqrt{2+c} &= 4\\
\end{align*}

Step 9:
Isolate the square root:  
\begin{align*}
\Rightarrow \qquad \sqrt{2+c} &= 2\\
\end{align*}

